# Happy Record Project Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
This is a React TypeScript monorepo for a pregnancy tracking app with desktop and mobile support. The project uses Lerna for package management and follows specific patterns for styling, theming, and internationalization.

## Styling Guidelines

### Theme Support
- **Always use CSS variables for colors** to support both light and dark themes
- Light theme variables are defined in: `packages/moon-ui/app-scss/theme/light.scss`
- Dark theme variables are defined in: `packages/moon-ui/app-scss/theme/dark.scss`
- Use `var(--variable-name)` syntax for all color values
- Example: `color: var(--text-color);` instead of `color: #000;`

### Spacing
- **Always use spacing utilities** from `packages/moon-ui/app-scss/metric.scss`
- Available spacing variables: `$spacing-xl`, `$spacing-lg`, `$spacing-md`, `$spacing-sm`, `$spacing-xs`, `$spacing-xxs`
- Use these for margin and padding only
- Example: `margin: $spacing-md;` instead of `margin: 12px;`

### Font Sizes
- **Always use the `toRem()` function** from `packages/moon-ui/app-scss/function.scss`
- Import: `@use '@moon-ui/app-scss/function' as *;`
- Example: `font-size: toRem(16px);` instead of `font-size: 16px;`

### SCSS Imports
Always include these imports at the top of SCSS files:
```scss
@use '@moon-ui/app-scss/metric' as *;
@use '@moon-ui/app-scss/function' as *;
```

## TypeScript Guidelines

### Type vs Interface
- **Prefer `type` over `interface`** for all type definitions
- Use `type` for object shapes, unions, intersections, and computed types
- Only use `interface` when you need declaration merging or extending

Example:
```typescript
// ✅ Good
type UserProps = {
  name: string;
  age: number;
};

// ❌ Avoid
interface UserProps {
  name: string;
  age: number;
}
```

## Component Structure

### Desktop and Mobile Support
- **Always create separate files** for desktop and mobile components
- File naming convention:
  - `component.desktop.tsx` - Desktop version
  - `component.mobile.tsx` - Mobile version
  - `component.desktop.module.scss` - Desktop styles
  - `component.mobile.module.scss` - Mobile styles
- Both versions should export the same component with the same props type

### Component Example Structure
```
src/
├── MyComponent.desktop.tsx
├── MyComponent.mobile.tsx
├── MyComponent.desktop.module.scss
├── MyComponent.mobile.module.scss
└── index.tsx (re-exports both versions)
```

### UIKit Components
- **All UI components must be under `packages/moon-ui/`**
- Follow the existing structure with separate folders for each component
- Each component should have its own `package.json`, TypeScript files, and SCSS files

## Internationalization

### Translation Hook
- **Always use `useIntl` hook** from `@dreamer/translation`
- Import: `import { useIntl } from '@dreamer/translation';`
- Usage: `const intl = useIntl();`
- Access translations: `intl.formatMessage({ id: 'translation.key' })`

### Translation Files
- **Always update both language files** when adding new translations:
  - `packages/translation/src/language/en.json` - English translations
  - `packages/translation/src/language/vi.json` - Vietnamese translations
- Use descriptive keys with dot notation: `ComponentName.actionName`
- Example: `"Button.submit": "Submit"`

### Translation Key Naming Convention
- Use PascalCase for component names
- Use camelCase for action descriptions
- Use descriptive, hierarchical keys
- Examples:
  - `"ChecklistTemplate.delete-confirm-title"`
  - `"CreateTask.label-submit"`
  - `"Button.primary"`

## Code Examples

### Component with Theme Support
```tsx
import React from 'react';
import { useIntl } from '@dreamer/translation';
import styles from './MyComponent.desktop.module.scss';

type MyComponentProps = {
  title: string;
  onAction: () => void;
};

const MyComponentDesktop = ({ title, onAction }: MyComponentProps) => {
  const intl = useIntl();
  
  return (
    <div className={styles.container}>
      <h2 className={styles.title}>{title}</h2>
      <button 
        className={styles.button}
        onClick={onAction}
      >
        {intl.formatMessage({ id: 'MyComponent.action' })}
      </button>
    </div>
  );
};

export default MyComponentDesktop;
```

### SCSS with Theme Variables
```scss
@use '@moon-ui/app-scss/metric' as *;
@use '@moon-ui/app-scss/function' as *;

.container {
  padding: $spacing-md;
  background: var(--card-background);
  border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
  border-radius: 8px;
}

.title {
  color: var(--text-title-primary-color);
  font-size: toRem(18px);
  font-weight: 600;
  margin-bottom: $spacing-sm;
}

.button {
  background: var(--button-default-background);
  color: var(--text-color-invert);
  border: none;
  padding: $spacing-sm $spacing-md;
  border-radius: 6px;
  font-size: toRem(14px);
  cursor: pointer;
  
  &:hover {
    background: var(--button-action-background);
    color: var(--button-action-color);
  }
}
```

### Translation Files Update
```json
// packages/translation/src/language/en.json
{
  "MyComponent.action": "Click Me",
  "MyComponent.title": "My Component"
}

// packages/translation/src/language/vi.json
{
  "MyComponent.action": "Nhấn Tôi",
  "MyComponent.title": "Thành Phần Của Tôi"
}
```

## File Organization

### Package Structure
```
packages/
├── moon-ui/                    # UI Kit components
│   └── component-name/
│       ├── package.json
│       ├── src/
│       │   ├── ComponentName.tsx
│       │   ├── ComponentName.module.scss
│       │   └── index.ts
├── page-ui/                    # Page components
│   └── page-name/
│       ├── package.json
│       └── src/
│           ├── index.desktop.tsx
│           ├── index.mobile.tsx
│           ├── index.desktop.module.scss
│           ├── index.mobile.module.scss
│           └── index.tsx
└── translation/                # Translation package
    └── src/
        └── language/
            ├── en.json
            └── vi.json
```

## Code Quality

### ESLint and Prettier
- **Always follow ESLint and Prettier rules** configured in the project
- Run `npm run lint` to check for ESLint errors before committing
- Run `npm run format` to format code with Prettier
- Fix all linting errors and warnings before submitting code
- The project uses pre-commit hooks to enforce code quality

## Best Practices

1. **Code Quality**: Always follow ESLint and Prettier rules
2. **Consistency**: Always follow the established patterns in the codebase
3. **Theme Support**: Never hardcode colors, always use CSS variables
4. **Responsive Design**: Create separate desktop and mobile versions
5. **Internationalization**: Always add translations for new text content
6. **Type Safety**: Use TypeScript types instead of interfaces
7. **Spacing**: Use the spacing utility variables for consistent spacing
8. **Font Sizes**: Use the `toRem()` function for responsive font sizing
9. **Component Organization**: Keep UI components in the moon-ui package
10. **Translation Keys**: Use descriptive, hierarchical key naming
11. **File Naming**: Follow the `.desktop.tsx` and `.mobile.tsx` convention

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

- ❌ Hardcoding colors instead of using CSS variables
- ❌ Using `interface` instead of `type`
- ❌ Not creating separate desktop/mobile files
- ❌ Forgetting to update translation files
- ❌ Using pixel values for spacing instead of spacing utilities
- ❌ Not using `toRem()` for font sizes
- ❌ Creating UI components outside of `packages/moon-ui/`
- ❌ Not using the `useIntl` hook for text content
